THE FINDING THAT BECAME A BOUND (M1, MEDIUM). inc/tagpu_hires.h said the macro's second consumer
"sizes the matching block" and that changing it fails spirv-check -- which invites regenerating
the SPIR-V and stopping. tagpu_vk_hires.c sizes nothing: VS_SZ 2480 / VS_PIECE 0 / VS_GAME 2304
are hand-copied literals and the macro is only the memcpy's bound. at 48 they agree with zero
slack (48*12*4 = 2304 = VS_GAME - VS_PIECE); at 64 the bound admits np = 64 into 2 480 bytes and
the copy writes 3 072, off the end of uPiece through the projection uniforms. fixed as a BOUND
rather than better prose -- a negative-array compile-time assertion (-std=c99, so no
_Static_assert), verified clean at 48 and failing at 64 with "size of array ... is negative"
naming the line. this is the only finding that changed what the code guarantees.

